    [2758] = {
        achievementId = 2758,
        name = "Argent Valor",
        category = "Argent Tournament",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Argent Valor",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete Aspirant training and multiple daily turn-ins for fifteen Aspirant's Seals.\n\n1. Enrol through The Argent Tournament introduction and finish the mounted combat lessons in your faction pavilion. Equip the supplied lance and use the stabled tournament mount; your ordinary travel mount is not the jousting vehicle.\n\n2. Accept Up to the Challenge and do all available Aspirant dailies: the field-kill task, Learning the Reins and the rotating weapon errand. A full day normally gives five Aspirant's Seals; fifteen are required, so plan multiple daily resets.\n\n3. Complete only today's weapon errand: A Blade Fit For A Champion uses Warts-B-Gone Lip Balm before EACH /kiss on a Lake Frog at Grizzly Hills 60.5, 51.5; speak to the revealed Maiden. A Worthy Weapon needs FOUR Winter Hyacinths from the Decrepit Flow (Crystalsong 12, 16), used inside the flower circle at Drak'Mar Lake (Dragonblight 93.1, 25.9); wait and LOOT the sword. The Edge of Winter needs Lord Everblaze's ember (Crystalsong 55.5, 74.9), used on the frozen Maiden at Winter's Breath Lake (Howling Fjord 42.2, 19.6). Return the obtained weapon to your own quest giver.\n\n4. For Learning the Reins, use the practice targets and each named vehicle ability required by the quest. Equip the lance and mount an eligible tournament steed. Build THREE Defend stacks (action 4) before challenging. Use Thrust (1) in melee; when the enemy rides away, Charge (3) as soon as range allows, then Shield-Breaker (2) while turning back to melee. Refresh Defend when a stack is lost. Heal between bouts.\n\n5. At fifteen Aspirant's Seals, finish Up to the Challenge and accept The Aspirant's Challenge. Speak to Squire David at the Aspirants' Ring while mounted with the lance equipped, then defeat the summoned Argent Valiant.\n\n6. Return to the pavilion and finish the promotion/invitation to the city offered to your character. This reaches Valiant and awards Argent Valor. You can begin the next rank's Valiant work as soon as it is offered; you do not need another fifteen Aspirant's Seals for each city.",
