    [2763] = {
        achievementId = 2763,
        name = "Exalted Champion of Ironforge",
        category = "Argent Tournament",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Exalted Champion of Ironforge",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete one city's Valiant training and challenge; Exalted variants also require that city's reputation grind.\n\n1. Reach Valiant through the Argent Aspiration/Argent Valor introduction. If Ironforge is not the first city offered to your character, finish that first city's championship before selecting another. Only ONE city's Valiant training can be active at a time.\n\n2. Speak to Lana Stouthammer in the Alliance pavilion at 76.4, 19.4 in Icecrown. Accept the invitation to represent Ironforge and The Valiant's Charge. Already being Exalted with the city does not replace the tournament training.\n\n3. Complete that city's available Valiant dailies: the weapon errand, A Valiant's Field Training, The Grand Melee and At the Enemy's Gates. Turn them in for Valiant's Seals and continue after daily resets until you have TWENTY-FIVE. Aspirant's Seals and Champion's Seals are different currencies/items.\n\n4. Complete only today's weapon errand: A Blade Fit For A Champion uses Warts-B-Gone Lip Balm before EACH /kiss on a Lake Frog at Grizzly Hills 60.5, 51.5; speak to the revealed Maiden. A Worthy Weapon needs FOUR Winter Hyacinths from the Decrepit Flow (Crystalsong 12, 16), used inside the flower circle at Drak'Mar Lake (Dragonblight 93.1, 25.9); wait and LOOT the sword. The Edge of Winter needs Lord Everblaze's ember (Crystalsong 55.5, 74.9), used on the frozen Maiden at Winter's Breath Lake (Howling Fjord 42.2, 19.6). Return the obtained weapon to your own quest giver.\n\n5. For field training, kill the requested eligible Scourge in Icecrown. For At the Enemy's Gates, take a provided campaign mount near the Court of Bones, maintain Defend, use Shield-Breaker on flyers and strip enemy riders' shields before charging. For The Grand Melee, defeat the requested city Valiants in the tournament rings. Equip the lance and mount an eligible tournament steed. Build THREE Defend stacks (action 4) before challenging. Use Thrust (1) in melee; when the enemy rides away, Charge (3) as soon as range allows, then Shield-Breaker (2) while turning back to melee. Refresh Defend when a stack is lost. Heal between bouts.\n\n6. Turn in the twenty-five seals to Lana Stouthammer, accept The Valiant's Challenge, then speak to Squire Danny at about 68.6, 20.9 while on the tournament mount with the lance equipped. Defeat his summoned Argent Champion; Danny does not start the bout for an ordinary unmounted visitor.\n\n7. Return to Lana Stouthammer and turn in the challenge to become Champion of Ironforge. Finish A Champion Rises when first offered. You retain earlier city championships when choosing a new Valiant city; the basic Champion achievement does not require Exalted.\n\n8. Also reach EXALTED with Ironforge on the character completing this city's championship. You can raise reputation before or after the challenge; both conditions are needed. Tournament dailies and Champion's Writ commendations help top up the bar.\n\n9. For a repeatable reputation route, buy the physical city tabard (45577) from Captain Stonehelm beside Ironforge's flight master at 55.6, 47.8 on the selected map. The current city purchase is a silver purchase and does not require Exalted or a championship. Check the tabard's own guide if a phased city vendor is missing.\n\n10. Equip that actual tabard, enter NORMAL Botanica in Netherstorm (71.7, 54.9), and clear enemies/bosses while checking Ironforge reputation. Use the exit behind Warp Splinter, reset outside and repeat, respecting the instance-entry limit. A transmog appearance alone gives no reputation.\n\n11. Confirm both Champion of Ironforge and Exalted Ironforge criteria. This awards Exalted Champion of Ironforge and its city title. It is one of the five city requirements toward Crusader; Argent Crusade Exalted is a separate final requirement.",
