        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Unlock the tournament vehicle and win a mounted player duel with another participant.\n\n1. Bring another player to the Argent Tournament. Both should complete enough introduction/training to use the stabled tournament mounts, and equip a lance. Winning against an NPC Valiant does not satisfy this player-duel achievement.\n\n2. Mount up near the tournament jousting rings, build three Defend stacks and use the vehicle's Duel action to challenge your friend. Win by reducing their vehicle's health with Thrust, Shield-Breaker and Charge. Refresh Defend during the duel.\n\n3. If the vehicle-duel countdown repeatedly dismounts both players, use the reported workaround: start an ordinary /duel on FOOT beside the stabled horses. Wait for the duel to actually begin, then the player needing credit mounts the tournament steed and the other player types /forfeit.\n\n4. Check the achievement, then swap roles if your friend also needs it. Use the workaround only if the normal mounted duel fails; simply fighting another outdoor player without the tournament vehicle is a different duel.",
        stepCount = 4,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 118, x = 0.75, y = 0.18, step = 1, label = "Tournament stables / Alliance jousting area" },
            { mapID = 118, x = 0.75, y = 0.26, step = 1, label = "Tournament stables / Horde jousting area" },
            { mapID = 118, x = 0.75, y = 0.18, step = 3, label = "If countdown dismounts you: start duel on foot, then mount" },
        },
        sources = {
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772#comments:id=676742",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772#comments:id=677491",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772#comments:id=2582662",
            "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772#comments:id=5164135",
        },
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2772#comments",
        difficultyReason = "Unlock the tournament vehicle and win a mounted player duel with another participant.",
        difficulty = "medium",
    },
    [2773] = {
        achievementId = 2773,
        name = "It's Just a Flesh Wound",
        category = "Argent Tournament",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "It's Just a Flesh Wound",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Finish the Black Knight investigation, obtain a city championship and complete the quest duel.\n\n1. Start Crusader Rhydalla's Black Knight investigation at the Argent pavilion (69.5, 23.1). For The Black Knight of Westfall? (Alliance), loot the Dusty Journal inside the house by its fireplace at Westfall 42.1, 69.7. For The Black Knight of Silverpine? (Horde), loot the journal inside the house at Silverpine Forest 53.2, 28.1. Return to Rhydalla.\n\n2. For The Seer's Crystal, kill Unbound Seers in Forlorn Woods, Crystalsong Forest (about 46, 40), until the crystal drops. The similarly named enemies in the Unbound Thicket are not the indicated farm. Return the crystal.\n\n3. For The Stories Dead Men Tell, visit the graveyard just east of the tournament (79.5, 23). Investigate the three named graves using the quest interaction/crystal: Sir Wendell Balfour, Lorien Sunblaze and Conall Irongrip. Return after all three credit.\n\n4. For There's Something About the Squire, kill a Skeletal Woodcutter near Crystalsong 38.3, 59.4 for a Large Femur. Use it on Maloric there to incapacitate him, search him for the Murderer's Toolkit and report back.\n\n5. For The Black Knight's Orders, use the Enchanted Bridle beside his gryphon at Icecrown 77.76, 21.62. Ride the gryphon to its destination so the ride objective credits, then loot BOTH items inside the house: invitation on a barrel, orders on crates beside the stove. Return to Rhydalla.\n\n6. Reach Champion rank for a city if the final quest is locked. Accept The Black Knight's Fall, equip the lance and use the STABLED ARGENT WARHORSE near the flight master (about 72.3, 22.5), rather than a racial tournament mount. Speak to Squire Cavin at the Ring of Champions to summon the Black Knight.\n\n7. Defeat the Black Knight and finish the quest turn-in with Rhydalla for the achievement. If he repeatedly evades at the vehicle transition, the comments' workaround is to dismount immediately after requesting the summon, BEFORE combat activates, equip your real weapon and kill him on foot once attackable. Repeatedly dismounting mid-fight can instead make him evade.",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
            {
