    [3142] = {
        achievementId = 3142,
        name = "Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings",
        category = "Raids",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Collect thirty Val'anyr fragments over weekly raids and complete the legendary's Yogg-Saron quest mechanics.\n\n1. Use a Paladin, Priest, Shaman, Monk, Druid or Evoker. Enter regular Ulduar in Storm Peaks and collect THIRTY Fragments of Val'anyr from eligible raid bosses over weekly resets. The present raid has one merged difficulty; the old separate 10/25-player selector is not the current route.\n\n2. Combine the 30 fragments into Shattered Fragments of Val'anyr and accept Ancient History from the item. After defeating the Assembly of Iron, use the Archivum Console in the room behind their arena. Complete that turn-in, accept Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings and receive the Unbound Fragments of Val'anyr quest item (45896).\n\n3. Continue through XT-002 and Kologarn, defeat Hodir, Thorim, Freya and Mimiron, then General Vezax. Leave at least ONE Keeper uninvited to Yogg-Saron. Asking only Thorim to assist is a straightforward setup; do not ask all four, because that removes the final phase's Deafening Roar.\n\n4. Enter Yogg-Saron's prison and keep the quest item ready. In phase 1, kill each arriving Guardian NEXT TO SARA so its death explosion damages her. Attacking Sara directly does not replace this mechanic. Repeat until Yogg appears and the tentacle/brain phase begins.\n\n5. Enter a brain portal, clear the illusion's tentacles and damage Yogg's brain to trigger the final phase. Leave through the exit portal BEFORE Induce Madness finishes; repeat the portal cycle if needed. Preserve your Sanity and turn away from gaze effects rather than staying in the brain room until the cast ends.\n\n6. In the final phase, KEEP YOGG ALIVE and face him when Deafening Roar begins. While he is actually casting it, target him and USE Unbound Fragments of Val'anyr (45896) to throw them into his mouth. After the successful throw, defeat and LOOT Yogg-Saron for the Reforged Hammer. A normal immediate boss kill cannot complete the throw.\n\n7. Return to the Archivum Console behind the Assembly of Iron arena, complete the quest, receive Val'anyr and EQUIP the finished mace for its wielder achievement. Collecting thirty fragments or completing the throw alone does not award ownership of the finished legendary.",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
            {
                mapID = 120,
                x = 0.41600000000000004,
                y = 0.182,
                step = 1,
                label = "Ulduar - fragment farming and legendary quest",
            },
            {
